e us some valuable  insight  um  and what we found was that uh of those  that were not yet vaccinated  that we spoke to people  knew where to receive a vaccine and  recognize it was an easy process if they  wanted to get a vaccine for themselves  um and of those who had not yet had the  vaccine roughly half of them had no  intention of getting the vaccine  and  some of the reasons cited were things  like uh health-related concerns or  distrust in the vaccine or that they'd  seen some negative news surrounding the  vaccine  so the findings of that survey will be  discussed further at the vaccine equity  group which we meet every week to  help improve vaccine access and  confidence and this will help  direct the team in terms of further  engagement activity going forwards  so those are the two things i wanted to  focus on from the engagement team i've  also got a short comms update from um  ellie caddick who is on league today but  she just wanted me to mention a few  points  so firstly um page is now live on the  ccg website to promote the walk-in  vaccination clinics  so and that is just being optimized at  the moment to make it uh make sure that  people find it very quickly when they  google  um but this page will be updated weekly  so that people get uh up-to-date  information on where the walk-in clinics  are in trafford the comps team are  looking to do some further outdoor  advertising in the north and central  areas to promote uptake to the under 30s  and also they'll be doing some  continuing with a digital advertising  campaign for the under 30s  which is directing people to the nhs  booking system and the final thing ellie  wanted me to mention was for 16 and 17  year olds the call to action is for  people to visit the national nhs  walk-in clinic page which has a search  engine uh to find clinics  for uh 16 or 17 year olds  although this information will also be  on the ccg  web page which i mentioned earlier  that's the update for me thank you uh  thank you nigel and and thank you for  covering um ellie's uh comms update  because i did actually how did he send  it to him and i was going to include it  at the end but you've stolen my thunder  on that one so thank you very much any  questions at all for uh nigel  yeah tell us accordingly um yeah i think  we're doing really well um  there's obviously a uh a section of the  community that are harder to get the  harder to lead to the vaccination center  i'm wondering um  i know it's  it sounds almost opportunistic  but we aren't expecting um  rates to go up when schools go back um  and in a sense are we able to ride that  wave are we in a position to sort of  really make one last push to try and get  some of those difficult um  people to get to the vaccination center  so it's really um  when rates go up are we able to sort of  say yeah rates are really  difficult now get that it's absolutely  definitely  necessary for you to get vaccinated at  this moment that's really all but i  think you're doing an excellent job  thanks  thank you council accordingly for that  um  i can echo exactly i do think an  excellent job has been done and uh and i  do know that we continue to strive  to get as many people vaccinated as  possible and that that work will  continue  i don't either oh yes counselor  blackburn thank you  thank you could i ask is there  any evidence as to which gender are not  wanting to be vaccinated either sort of  one or the other  and secondly it's probably for you know  for ellie maybe to take up um would  manu lancashire crickets or altering mfc  consider um doing something prior to  kickoff and encouraging people to get  vaccinated who haven't been thank you  eleanor is that something we can we can  look at  yes we certainly can and we we um i  think that's a really good idea asking  them to do that encouragement i think  with some of the people now who are  choosing not to be vaccinated it is a  very active choice  um we've made you know vaccination is  very available and we've really been  pushing it very very hard the ccg has  been working tremendously hard on this  um including you know direct contact  from gps and so on so for some people  there is just a huge suspicion of the  vaccination and and huge anxieties about  it and to be fair i think you know with  those people it's  really you're not we're not going to  change their mind at this point what we  need to do is just make sure everybody  knows that should their minds change  it's available to them but jill has been  working on this more specifically so i  think she'll be able to answer more of  um those points so jilla  thanks yeah so just to respond to the  first part of your question counselor  blackburn um it was just a pilot and so  the numbers were quite small  uh i think too small for us to really be  able to say if there was a real gender  difference but now that we've completed  the pilot and taken some learning from  that we do  intend to  roll that out more widely and survey  other areas  so that will increase our sample size  and  therefore you know the robustness of the  data and we might then be able to drill  down to subgroups and  and have that level of understanding but  there wasn't anything jumping out from  the pilot that indicated there was an  imbalance between uh men and women on  vaccine hesitancy and as i say we will  be rolling it out further  thank you chiller um  just coming back to council blackmon's  point about manchester united and and  the cricket i can tell you that i have i  do know two people who both double  vaccinated they went to the first game  at manchester united and they have both  come down with kobe 19 and one of them  has been very poorly  um so it is you know in the i would  argue in the club's interest perhaps  help us along those lines if we can  possibly get them to do some  announcements that'll be really useful  any further questions at all  well that brings us to the the end of  the agenda the next meeting is on the  8th of september and i'm going to offer  my apologies now because i will be on  annual leave and i've arranged for alex  to contact george devlin so i think  we'll be back to chair the next meeting  for us so i'll i'm off for a fortnight  from friday  and  just continue to enjoy this the summer  and i i i'm rather reliably informed the  sun is definitely coming out this week  elena  thank you very much for your attendance  thank you i'll hold you to that  okay  bye
 

